  expReward: 150
  offerDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - The old delivery road is gone, but Grandma Susan is still waiting for this
      crate.
    - Our first obstacle is a short canyon. Build a beam bridge, then carry the crate
      across yourself.
    - A drawing can look safe. The delivery test will prove whether it really is.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - A beam bridge carries the load along its road and into the supports on both
      banks.
    - Keep the route continuous. You will be walking every step of it with the cargo
      in your hands.
    - When the bridge is ready, press Simulate, pick up the crate, and place it at
      the marked handoff point across the canyon.
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - Grandma Susan's crate is still on this side of the canyon.
    - Enter the Blueprint, finish the bridge, then press Simulate and deliver it
      to the marked handoff point.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Professor Bhan
    sentences:
    - First crossing complete. More importantly, the crate made it across intact.
    - Good work, {PlayerName}. Grandma Susan is one bridge closer to receiving her
      supplies.
    - Take a moment to review the bridge in your Almanac, then we will continue the
      delivery.
